    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0302" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg246"/>

                <head>No. 134.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Hoffman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 27,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram received. Sir Edward Thornton has read to me one from Lord Derby,
                    stating that you had proposed to him the negotiation of the additional
                    article.</p>
                <p>You will please inform me immediately whether the suggestion proceeded in the
                    first instance from you or from him, and if from him, how far you may have
                    encouraged it.</p>
                <closer><signed>FISH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
